fn parse_usize(s: &str, name: &str) -> usize {
    // This is handled by clap? Actually we parse manually after clap to get same error messages?
    // Instead, let clap parse as String and we parse here to control error? But clap can parse directly with value_parser.
    // For identical clap error messages, we should use value_parser with usize.
    // However, our build_cli currently doesn't set value_parser, so values are Strings.
    // We need to set value_parser to get clap's invalid digit / too large errors.
    // Let's instead set value_parser in build_cli.
    // This function is fallback.
